    title: "Federal Executive Council",
    description:
      "Executive power is shared among a council rather than concentrated in a single president, preventing any one person from wielding unchecked authority.",
  },
  {
    number: "03",
    title: "Federal Government Taxes States",
    description:
      "The federal government raises revenue by levying on state governments, not citizens directly, so federal taxation must pass through a democratic filter.",
  },
  {
    number: "04",
    title: "Supermajority Lawmaking Rules",
    description:
